* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-postlayout-pex-pvt (issue #30, Part of #16)
* SCHEMATIC-LEVEL control arm for the post-layout charge-pump comparison.
*
* This is ../../sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim/testbench/tb_cp_dc.sp.tmpl with NO
* deliberate difference at all: same corner library, same `.option scale=1`,
* same four ideal trim-code reference currents into the block's own on-chip
* cascode bias replica, same compliance sweep, same `i(Vout)` sign
* convention. It is duplicated into this record rather than invoked in place
* only so that both arms of this comparison are driven by one run script and
* one host, which is the whole point of having a control arm: the deviation
* this record analyses must be "what did the extracted interconnect do", not
* "what did a different host/ngspice do".
*
* That this arm reproduces the committed
* ../../sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim/corners/results.csv is itself checked and
* reported -- see ../records/RECORD-001.

.option scale=1

.include cp_snap.spice

Vdd VDD 0 dc 3.3

* .subckt cp UP DN IBP ICP IBN ICN VOUT VDD VSS
XCP up dn ibp icp ibn icn vout VDD 0 cp

Irefbp ibp 0 dc 10u
Irefcp icp 0 dc 10u
Irefbn 0 ibn dc 10u
Irefcn 0 icn dc 10u

Vup up 0 dc 0
Vdn dn 0 dc 0
Vout vout 0 dc 1.65

